<decision #track.execute-ai-data-workflow-through-eidolon-runtime.driver-boundary apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M05F1PQ64H8AW8H0ZD162XFA>
  Which layer owns mutable DAG semantics and which layer drives effects?
  </?01M05F1PQ64H8AW8H0ZD162XFA>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M05F1PQ64H8AW8H0ZD162XFB>
    depa-flows owns RunGraph semantics; Eidolon owns host application and effect authorities.
    </?01M05F1PQ64H8AW8H0ZD162XFB>
    <decision-text ?01M05F1PQ64H8AW8H0ZD162XFC>
    Use canonical graph/patch/invalidation/reuse functions and add only a persisted Eidolon driver over their ready frontier.
    </?01M05F1PQ64H8AW8H0ZD162XFC>
    <rationale ?01M05F1PQ64H8AW8H0ZD162XFD>
    This preserves product semantics without introducing a parallel workflow core.
    </?01M05F1PQ64H8AW8H0ZD162XFD>
  )>
)>
